# ISRG Root YR, cross-signed by ISRG Root X1.
#
# Why this file exists:
#   asuci.uci.edu and internal.studentgov.uci.edu serve an incomplete chain -
#   leaf plus the "Let's Encrypt YR1" intermediate, and nothing linking YR1's
#   issuer (ISRG Root YR) to a root in Mozilla's bundle. Browsers and Windows
#   recover by fetching the missing certificate over AIA; OpenSSL does not, so
#   requests fails on Linux CI with "unable to get local issuer certificate".
#
#   Supplying this cross-signed certificate completes the path:
#       leaf -> Let's Encrypt YR1 -> ISRG Root YR -> ISRG Root X1
#   ISRG Root X1 is the trust anchor and comes from certifi, so verification is
#   still full and still terminates at a Mozilla-trusted root. Certificate
#   verification is never disabled.
#
# Provenance: downloaded 2026-08-12 from http://yr.i.lencr.org/, the CA Issuers
#   AIA URI published by the YR1 intermediate. Subject "C=US, O=ISRG, CN=Root YR",
#   issuer "C=US, O=Internet Security Research Group, CN=ISRG Root X1".
#
# Remove this file once certifi ships ISRG Root YR, or once the sites serve a
# complete chain; asuci/tests cover the verification path either way.
